forbid ordered args

require: (input, context) => {} pattern

never allow ordered args

reasons: key-value inputs for readability, observability, evolvability

inputs: one key-value object + context object

## .exemption = single-value transformers
single-value transformer prefixes (as*, is*) may take their one value positionally
- one input by definition (asFoo(x)/asFooFromBar(bar)/isBar(x)); named wrapper earns keep only on multi-arg
- e.g. asDeclaredAwsIamPolicyStatement(statement), asZoneAddress(raw) = fine
- still required for 2+ inputs or optional config — even a transformer once it grows a second arg

enforcement:
- as*/is* transformer with exactly one positional value = allowed
- transformer with 2+ inputs passed positionally = blocker